{"model":"gpt-6-luna","messages":[{"role":"system","content":"You are a planning specialist.\nCreate a dense markdown plan with explicit checkpoints and tool-aware execution steps.\nUse discovery tools (`bash`, `search_files`, `list_dir`) to inspect local context if needed.\nUse `bash` with `rg` for fast discovery when helpful.\nDo not implement changes.\n\nParent execution tools (must be respected by the final plan): read_file\nAll execution steps in the final plan must be feasible using only those parent tools."},{"role":"user","content":"Goal\nPrepare a realistic plan for a small documentation update about planning capability in this repository, then execute only the analysis portion and report a concise proposal covering purpose, configuration options, and example usage.\n\nContext\nThe repository should be inspected to identify the planning capability, its implementation\/configuration, existing documentation conventions, and a suitable documentation location. The user explicitly requests: first create a plan; then execute only its analysis part. Do not implement the documentation update.\n\nConstraints\n- Planner subagent may use bash\/search for discovery.\n- Parent execution tools after planning: only read_file.\n- Do not modify any files.\n- Final response under 180 words.\n- Plan should distinguish analysis from later writing\/review work; only analysis is executed now.\n\nExpected Outcomes\nA practical staged plan for a small docs update, plus evidence-based concise proposal outlines for (1) capability purpose, (2) configuration options, and (3) example usage.\n\nAcceptance Criteria\n- Planning occurs before repository analysis.\n- Analysis identifies relevant implementation\/configuration and docs context without edits.\n- Final response clearly labels the three requested outlines and notes that no files were changed.\n- Final response is under 180 words."}],"parallel_tool_calls":false,"max_completion_tokens":1024,"tools":[{"type":"function","function":{"name":"read_file","description":"Read the contents of a file with line numbers. Use to examine file content after finding it with search_files.\n\nExamples:\n- \"composer.json\" \u2192 read composer.json from project root\n- \"src\/Config.php\" \u2192 read specific file by path\n- {\"path\": \"large.log\", \"offset\": 100, \"limit\": 50} \u2192 read lines 101-150\n\nReturns numbered lines. By default, output is limited to 200 lines or 32 KiB, whichever comes first.\nSet larger limit and max_bytes values when a larger window or the complete file is justified.\nWhen more content exists, the result includes the exact offset or bash command needed to continue.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string","description":"File path (relative to project root or absolute). Example: \"composer.json\" or \"src\/Config.php\""},"offset":{"type":"integer","description":"Line number to start reading from (0-indexed)"},"limit":{"type":"integer","description":"Maximum number of lines to read (default: 200; no fixed upper limit)"},"max_bytes":{"type":"integer","description":"Maximum output bytes (default: 32768; increase explicitly for a larger or full-file read)"}},"required":["path"],"additionalProperties":false}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"bash","description":"Execute a bash command and return bounded stdout\/stderr. Use for shell operations, not file reading.\n\nExamples:\n- \"git status\" \u2192 check git state\n- \"composer install\" \u2192 install dependencies\n- \"php artisan migrate\" \u2192 run migrations\n- \"grep -r 'TODO' src\/\" \u2192 search file contents\n- \"npm run build\" \u2192 run build scripts\n\nPrefer dedicated file tools over cat, sed-based rewrites, and shell redirection.\nIf output is truncated, narrow the command or redirect it to a file and inspect it with the dedicated read tool.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"command":{"type":"string","description":"The bash command to execute"}},"required":["command"],"additionalProperties":false}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"search_files","description":"Search for files by name\/path pattern (not content). Returns matching file paths.\n\nExamples:\n- \"composer.json\" \u2192 finds composer.json recursively in all directories\n- \"*.php\" \u2192 finds PHP files in root directory only\n- \"**\/*.php\" \u2192 finds PHP files recursively in all directories\n- \"src\/**\/*.php\" \u2192 finds PHP files recursively under src\/\n- \".\/composer.json\" \u2192 finds composer.json in root directory only\n- \"Config\" \u2192 finds files with \"Config\" in their name, recursively\n\nNote: Use read_file to examine file contents after finding them.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"pattern":{"type":"string","description":"Search pattern. Examples: \"composer.json\" (recursive), \"**\/*.php\" (recursive glob), \"*.json\" (root only), \".\/README.md\" (exact path)"},"patterns":{"type":"array","description":"Multiple patterns to search at once. Example: [\"composer.json\", \"package.json\", \"*.xml\"]","items":{"type":"string"}}},"additionalProperties":false}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"list_dir","description":"List directory contents. Shows files and subdirectories with [file] or [dir] markers.\n\nExamples:\n- \".\" or \"\" \u2192 list project root\n- \"src\" \u2192 list src directory\n- \"packages\/addons\/src\" \u2192 list nested directory\n\nUse to explore project structure before searching for specific files.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string","description":"Directory path. Examples: \".\" (root), \"src\", \"packages\/addons\""}},"required":["path"],"additionalProperties":false}}}],"tool_choice":"auto","reasoning_effort":"none"}